-- Migration 2 → 3: where a session happens.
--
-- Adds a coordinate to the session, so sunrise, sunset, and the golden hours can be
-- computed for the place the shoot is actually at. The maths is offline — see
-- `core:common`'s SolarCalculator — so this is the only thing standing between a studio
-- and knowing when the light goes on a moor with no signal.
--
-- Nullable, because most sessions will never carry one: a studio portrait needs no sun
-- position, and demanding a coordinate to save a session would be friction charged to
-- every booking to serve the few that shoot outdoors.
--
-- Purely additive. Two nullable columns on an existing table, so every row a studio
-- already has survives untouched with both columns null.
--
-- These statements must produce exactly the schema the .sq files describe; the
-- verifyMigrations task compares the two and fails the build if they diverge.

ALTER TABLE session ADD COLUMN latitude REAL;
ALTER TABLE session ADD COLUMN longitude REAL;
